# A6L power28 (28 Sep 2026): HVDCP / Quick Charge 2.0+3.0 for the PM660 SMB2 (applies on top of qcom_smbx-a6l-fcc-jeita.patch).
# Default hvdcp_enable=0 = register-identical to r4. Params: hvdcp_enable (0644), hvdcp_max_uv (<= 9 V), hvdcp_icl_ua (0644, <= 2 A),
# hvdcp_status (ro). Details: docs/fastcharge-20260928.md. Host test: power/test/hvdcp/run-hvdcp-sim.sh.
# power29 (29 Sep 2026): APSD poll window re-armed at every plug-in, DCP/OCP/FLOAT handled alike (OCP/FLOAT logged: D+/D-
# disturbed, e.g. USB gadget pull-up), APSD changes logged, wait for QC_AUTH_DONE, hvdcp_rerun (0200) + hvdcp_regs (0444).
# Details: docs/fastcharge2-20260929.md.
# r5 bug hunt power (29 Sep 2026): (a) the abort path's USBIN suspend (adapter still > 6 V after FORCE_5V) is released at
# the unplug (hv_susp; only when the driver itself set it: a suspend written by userspace, e.g. a6l-chg-guard, is never
# taken over, and a userspace STATUS write hands the bit back to userspace), also after hvdcp_enable=0; before, the next
# charger never charged until reboot. (b) the usb-plugin IRQ kicks the HVDCP work at the edge: a replug inside the 1.5 s
# status-work delay / before the 2 s failed-state poll no longer carries the failed state (500 mA, no retry) to the next
# cable. hvdcp_enable=0 and idle: no change (A6L_HVDCP_OFF_TRACE SAME). Sim scenarios 24-27 (power/test/hvdcp).
